`permutation_familywise_separation_auc` tests trajectory separation over a family of results (such as one per frequency band, built from the same trials) and several contrasts. Each permutation draws one within-subject relabelling and applies it to every result and contrast, and each observed AUC gets a family-wise p-value from the maximum-AUC null. `permutation_null_separation_auc` now returns its p-value as a third value, `(observed, null, p_value)`, and keeps every permutation in the null. `permute_labels_within_strata` moved to `coco_pipe.utils` so both decoding and dim_reduction use it; `coco_pipe.decoding` still exports it.
